The static gate is now decisive: the clean fixed semantics proves that each one-element loop leaves `value = 2` and rejects `99`, while the candidate’s proof-local theory proves the false result `99` for both exact loop bodies on the same valid integer input `[2]`. The two priority-40 summaries erase an arbitrary continuation-visible binding update, with no bridge-free connection theorem.

I’ve also completed the 949-entry source inventory (including zero simplification/functional rules and all 25 opaque symbols). I’m proceeding with the separate required false-postcondition mutation now; this tests result constraint independently of the bridge-context counterexample.
